\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces The branch of cycles observed against the choke opening (seventeen transients from the blocked state, last \SI {8000}{\second } of \SI {16000}{\second }): (a) range and mean of the flowline inlet pressure, with the steady state along the opening, solid where it is linearly stable (up to $a = 0.13$) and dashed where it is unstable; (b) interval between blowdowns, the two values where blowouts alternate, with the periods of the two complex pairs of the linearised steady state where they are close to or beyond the imaginary axis: the oscillation of the liquid column of the riser on the gas pocket of the flowline (a manometer-like mode of about \SI {70}{\second }, linearly unstable from $a = 0.13$ but never seen in the transients) and the slow exchange of liquid between flowline and riser (500 to \SI {1000}{\second }, the mode that becomes the cycle), evaluated at the openings of the continuation (small marks) and involving no simulation; (c) peak (dot) and mean (dash) liquid flow rate through the choke, on a logarithmic axis; (d) how far the gas penetrates the riser in a cycle: the lowest position of the top of the liquid column, as a fraction of the riser height (1: the column always reaches the top; 0: the riser is blown out completely). Colour: class of the cycle; squares: blowouts alternating in size (periodic at 0.70, intervals not repeating within the run from 0.80).}}{21}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:branch}{{9}{21}{The branch of cycles observed against the choke opening (seventeen transients from the blocked state, last \SI {8000}{\second } of \SI {16000}{\second }): (a) range and mean of the flowline inlet pressure, with the steady state along the opening, solid where it is linearly stable (up to $a = 0.13$) and dashed where it is unstable; (b) interval between blowdowns, the two values where blowouts alternate, with the periods of the two complex pairs of the linearised steady state where they are close to or beyond the imaginary axis: the oscillation of the liquid column of the riser on the gas pocket of the flowline (a manometer-like mode of about \SI {70}{\second }, linearly unstable from $a = 0.13$ but never seen in the transients) and the slow exchange of liquid between flowline and riser (500 to \SI {1000}{\second }, the mode that becomes the cycle), evaluated at the openings of the continuation (small marks) and involving no simulation; (c) peak (dot) and mean (dash) liquid flow rate through the choke, on a logarithmic axis; (d) how far the gas penetrates the riser in a cycle: the lowest position of the top of the liquid column, as a fraction of the riser height (1: the column always reaches the top; 0: the riser is blown out completely). Colour: class of the cycle; squares: blowouts alternating in size (periodic at 0.70, intervals not repeating within the run from 0.80)}{figure.9}{}}
