\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Gas lift with the choke open at the base point, from the blocked state, for gas pressures at the platform from \SI {20}{\bar  } (valve closed: the base case) to \SI {150}{\bar  }: (a) flowline inlet pressure; (b) bottom-hole pressure; (c) gas injected through the check valve; (d) liquid rate through the choke, on a logarithmic axis; (e) mean liquid holdup of the riser. The oscillation of (d) from \SI {130}{\bar  }, which dies out after \SI {1500}{\second } at 130, after \SI {4000}{\second } at 140 and persists at \SI {150}{\bar  }, is the pattern switching of the two horizontal cells at the top of the riser discussed in the text.}}{23}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
